        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Conspirare, Royal Opera House\n- People: Eric Whitacre, Tarik O'Regan, David Lang, Jocelyn Hagen, Donald Grantham, Nico Muhly, Mark Adamo, Robert Kyr, Jake Heggie, Eric Banks, Jake Runestad, Edward Dick, Benjamin Britten\n- Products: Tarik O'Regan: Threshold of Night\n- Projects: Virtual Choir\n- Places: Aldeburgh, London\n- Topics: commissioned choral works, opera productions\n\nFacts:\n- In 2008, Edward Dick directed Benjamin Britten's opera \"The Rape of Lucretia\" at Aldeburgh.\n- In 2011, Edward Dick directed a new opera by Tarik O'Regan at the Royal Opera House in London.\n- Eric Whitacre, born on January 2, 1970, is a Grammy-winning American composer, conductor, and speaker known for choral, orchestral, and wind ensemble music.\n- Eric Whitacre is also known for his Virtual Choir projects, which combine individual voices from around the world into an online choir.\n- Conspirare has commissioned works from composers including David Lang, Tarik O'Regan, Jocelyn Hagen, Donald Grantham, Eric Whitacre, Nico Muhly, Mark Adamo, Robert Kyr, Jake Heggie, Eric Banks, and Jake Runestad.\n- Tarik O'Regan: Threshold of Night is the third release by Conspirare and the second recording of the work of Tarik O'Regan.",
